      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In developing a treatment plan for elderly patients with ischemic heart disease, it is important to appreciate that the pathophysiologic process and aging influence the type of response produced by various drugs. The aging process also alters the way drugs are absorbed, distributed, and eliminated. Each of these variables must be considered in deciding which drugs should be used and how they should be administered."},
